# Cursor / IDE index scope.
#
# Everything listed here is excluded from the IDE index, which means it also
# stays out of the agent's context window. The repository is 1060 tracked
# files; a lane that needs five of them should not be paying for a thousand.
#
# Two rules for editing this file:
#   1. Never exclude a path an agent may legitimately need to READ. Excluded
#      files are invisible to the agent, not merely unindexed - a wrong entry
#      here looks exactly like "the file does not exist".
#   2. Per-lane narrowing does NOT belong here. Use git sparse-checkout in that
#      lane's worktree instead, so the files are genuinely absent from disk.
#      See ops/director/BOLT_DIRECTOR_STATE.json for the current lane sets.

# Environments and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Heavy archives, dumps and logs
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.log
logs/

# Static and build output
staticfiles/
media/
node_modules/

# Other agents' working copies. Each worktree is a full checkout of this same
# repository; indexing them multiplies every file by the number of worktrees.
.audit-worktrees/
.ember-worktrees/
.claude/worktrees/
.audit-runtime/

# Throwaway agent working files. Regenerated constantly, never reviewed.
scratchpad/
ops/audits/

# Historical evidence. AGENTS.md section 10 makes archived material
# non-authoritative for design, so it must not compete for context.
docs/agents/memory/source_prompts/
